cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these rules or texts, please cite them as below and name the rules revision you used."
title: "Studiolo: the tarot games of the 1787 Turin rulebook"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Tsaplin"
    given-names: "Evgeny"
    affiliation: "Petri Games"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7231-483X"
abstract: >-
  Machine-readable and plain-English rules of the tarot card games of the Turin rulebook
  «Primi elementi e regole del giuoco de' tarocchi» (Torino, Soffietti, 1787). Every rule carries its
  source, its page and a mark: documented, our reading, or sources silent. With the journal of
  revisions, the list of open questions and the method. With the rules engine, bots and the tools to
  measure them.
keywords:
  - tarot
  - tarocchi
  - card games
  - trick-taking games
  - history of games
  - Piedmont
  - rules reconstruction
